    "collected_at": "2026-11-12T14:05:33.359732+00:00",
    "origin_id": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/this-low-profile-motorhome-is-the-smallest-of-its-kind-but-unbelievably-elegant-278328.html",
    "canonical_url": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/this-low-profile-motorhome-is-the-smallest-of-its-kind-but-unbelievably-elegant-278328.html",
    "origin_publisher": "autoevolution",
    "published_at": "2026-11-12T14:01:12+00:00",
    "published_at_raw": "2026-11-12T14:01:12+0000",
    "publication_precision": "TIMESTAMP",
    "acquired_at": "2026-11-12T14:06:40.664595+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-12T14:06:40.664595+00:00",
    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Honda CRF1150L Africa Twin Enduro Sports Is a Tongue Twister, Weighs Less but Offers More\nThis Low-Profile Motorhome Is the Smallest of Its Kind but Unbelievably Elegant\n18 photos\nPhoto: Kabe AB\nLow-volume RV specialist Kabe AB says they're \"always a step ahead,\" presumably of the competition. The Novum c720 LGB motorhome isn't highlighted as an example of what makes them different from the rest, but it probably should be.\nThis is the smallest motorhome on offer from Kabe , with the original floorplan introduced a couple of years back under the longer name Novum Compact 720 LGB. For 2027, the model comes with a simplified name and a refreshed interior that brings it, despite the comparatively smaller dimensions, on equal footing with its bigger siblings.\nKabe is a name that probably won't ring many bells for readers outside of Europe. Based in Sweden, it's more of a boutique-style manufacturer of travel trailers and motorhomes, both low profile and fully integrated, that stand out for their sleek, elegant style and quality work.\nKabe products are more expensive than average; they might even be described as pricey among their premium peers, but they're built almost entirely in-house, which ensures excellent quality control. They delivery the quality, the functionality, and the looks, and the same also applies to this compact motorhome.\nPhoto: Kabe AB The Novum c720 LGB is the smallest of the Novums . It comes in at 7.16 meters (23.5 feet) of total length and 2.24 meters (7.3 feet) of width, and it's offered standard with a maximum permissible weight of 3,500 kg (7,716 lbs), which means you can still operate it on a standard B Category driving license without needing to upgrade.\nLike all Novum or, for that matter, Kabe motorhomes, this one sits on a Mercedes-Benz Sprinter chassis, offered standard with a 9-speed automatic transmission and all the extra features that are standard, including a backup camera. The interior, on the other hand, is purely Kabe, with gorgeous cabinetry and elegant finishes.\nThe layout doesn't do much in terms of breaking the mold of interior compact RV design , but the style elevate it into a class of its own. The shell comes with sandwich construction and Ecoprim insulation in the floor, ceiling, and walls, so this is a motorhome that will remain as comfortable in sub-freezing temperatures as it will be in hot weather.\nPhoto: Kabe AB Inside, the walls are covered in breathable, soft-touch fabrics of different textures and colors to match each separate space. For instance, in the bedroom, you have an intimate alcove vibe with dark padded walls that match the headboard, while in the dining area, the fabrics are lighter in color and style.\nThe layout puts a convertible dinette at the front, under a large, curbed skylight, a galley kitchen in the middle of the RV with a wet bathroom across, and the bedroom at the back. To be able to offer a rear pass-through garage that would fit personal luggage as well as adventure gear like a pair of bicycles, Kabe lifts the beds in the bedroom on a platform, creating more headroom underneath.\nThen, in the garage, they add metal shelving, netted cubbies, more shelves of wood, and tie-downs on the walls and on the floor. A pass-through garage under an elevated bed is not new, but out of all of them, this is perhaps the neatest, best organized around. And that 's the Kabe difference.\nPhoto: Kabe AB Upstairs in the bedroom, you have two longitudinal single beds on an aluminum frame that you can join by pulling out an extension and adding inserts into a king bed. You have two more skylights here for ventilation and natural light to offset the darkness of the walls, wraparound cabinetry , prep for a second TV, and beautiful accent lighting.\nAdditional storage space is built into the base of the beds, in the form of two wardrobes.\nAt the front, the dinette uses face-to-face benches and the swiveling captain seats to create a space that could accommodate up to five people around the two-fold adjustable table. Overhead cabinets with curved faces and real wood construction, open cubbies in the driver's cab, and prep for a TV on the wall by the door are standard.\nPhoto: Kabe AB The kitchen is compact, as is customary in Europe – and specced with the basics. A two-burner gas cooktop and a stainless sink under separate glass covers, a Thetford fridge with freezer, an extractor, and lots of drawers and cubbies with central locking are all included.\nUnlike in other European motorhomes, the kitchen is as elegant as the rest of the spaces, and because of it, an integral part of them.\nThe bathroom is located right across from the fridge and wardrobe, and it's a wet one. It's larger than you'd expect, though, with a nice shower column, a cassette toilet, and a fold-down sink masked behind a mirror under the medicine cabinet. It's also more elegant than you'd probably expect, too.\nPhoto: Kabe AB Standard features include Alde 3030 heating with underfloor heating, a 230W 3kW 3-stage electric heater in the bathroom, the digital command panel Kabe does in-house, a 100Ah leisure battery, remote-controlled central locking, and fully winterized plumbing. The motorhome can hold 130 liters (34 gallons) of freshwater and 90 liters (24 gallons) of gray in a heated tank.\nKabe lists a mass in running order of 2,945 kg (6,492 lbs), with a maximum permissible weight of 3,500 kg (7,716 lbs). You can, however, upgrade that to 4,500 kg (9,921 lbs) but, in that case, you'd no longer be able to drive it on a B Category license.\nPhoto: Kabe AB The base price for the 2027 Novum c720 LGB is €132,000, which is approximately $146,300 at the current exchange rate. The unit brought out on display at the 2026 Dusseldorf Caravan Salon, which you can see in the second video at the bottom of the page, had a sticker of €147,990 ($164,000) with options.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nKabe Kabe Novum motorhome luxury RVs mercedes-benz sprinter Europe RV\nAbout the author: Elena Gorgan\nElena has been writing for a living since 2006 and, as a journalist, she has put her double major in English and Spanish to good use. She covers automotive and mobility topics like cars and bicycles, and she always knows the shows worth watching on Netflix and friends. Full profile\nUP NEXT Xiaomi Appears To Have Run Out of Steam, Despite Promising SkyNomad Sales in October",
